      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">What dental services do you provide? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>We provide a full range of dental services including cleanings, fillings, tooth extractions, root canal treatments, braces, crowns, veneers, teeth whitening, dentures, implants, and smile makeovers. We also specialize in orofacial pain management for headaches, migraines, TMJ disorders, and facial pain.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">Is tooth extraction painful? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Not at all! Extractions are performed under local anesthesia, and we ensure you're comfortable throughout the process. Most patients feel only mild pressure, not pain. We also offer post-extraction care instructions and follow-up to ensure smooth healing.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">What are veneers and laminates? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Veneers and laminates are thin shells placed over teeth to fix discoloration, chips, gaps, or slight misalignments — giving you a brighter, even smile. They are custom-made for each patient and bonded permanently to the front surface of teeth.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">When is a root canal needed? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>A root canal is needed when a tooth's nerve is infected or damaged due to deep decay, trauma, or cracks. It helps save the natural tooth and relieves pain caused by infection. Symptoms include severe toothache, prolonged sensitivity, and gum swelling.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">Do you handle dental emergencies? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, we handle dental emergencies such as severe toothaches, broken teeth, knocked-out teeth, and injuries. Just call us at +91 99620 02537 and we'll ensure you're treated as soon as possible with same-day appointments when needed.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-question">Do you treat headaches and facial pain? <span class="faq-icon"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes! As an orofacial pain clinic, we diagnose and treat tension headaches, migraines, TMJ/TMD disorders, trigeminal neuralgia, and undiagnosed facial pains. We use advanced diagnostic tools to identify the root cause and create personalized treatment plans.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
